{
  "step_1": "The decision reason can be applied to the decision problem. The reason focuses on the outcomes of each lottery and considers differences between outcomes as negligible. Here, Lottery A offers 500 Euros with 100% probability, and Lottery B offers 1000 Euros with 50% probability or 0 Euros with 50% probability. The outcomes differ (500 vs. 1000 or 0), but if these differences are considered negligible, the reason would focus on the probability of obtaining a favorable outcome. A 'favorable outcome' is not explicitly defined, but under the assumption that any positive outcome is favorable, Lottery A has a 100% chance of a positive outcome, while Lottery B has a 50% chance. Thus, the reason would prefer Lottery A due to its higher probability of a favorable (i.e., positive) outcome.",
